tion/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the constant multiple rule for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot (1)-y\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-159616/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53c5d5d7-40d4-5210-8794-428cffc1f3f9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159616"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159585/selection/b5be7d38503dcbf1896dc73e5bd6ccf72db0ba1c926b6910aad76337483f2ff5" :answer/id #uuid "ebc985d9-e589-5b8f-9e06-aeb0e64df5fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159585/selection/60819bd46c55f03aebf83342c83b88fdef35056fd30a3a6f9b2b5184b8300f58" :answer/id #uuid "d563e186-6da0-52b0-bd08-cde35c49f5ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{\\pi }^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159585/selection/bf9da5eda33b0747c85c14cc2637fcb08975b2c6444398dcd67c40e1863751f8" :answer/id #uuid "0b8135fd-0ca3-5b70-ab1b-9ccdad130fc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\pi }^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159585/selection/8d9781a51683d91d91197841e9e786096d99194e4b76add95275d4c164799e4f" :answer/id #uuid "36326366-e9d9-51ca-a920-8eda10f515c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\pi -1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159585/selection/9b49ed1a91e9087b6b2cc4f15092d29a6f833d1b3fe90395a973a4df3f6d0b57" :answer/id #uuid "4df1f15d-897a-52aa-9ecd-9da536e2c2ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi +1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159585/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ab8ea4e-2381-5789-addf-372771f8a602" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159585/selection/8d9781a51683d91d91197841e9e786096d99194e4b76add95275d4c164799e4f" :answer-field/choices ["q-159585/selection/b5be7d38503dcbf1896dc73e5bd6ccf72db0ba1c926b6910aad76337483f2ff5" "q-159585/selection/60819bd46c55f03aebf83342c83b88fdef35056fd30a3a6f9b2b5184b8300f58" "q-159585/selection/bf9da5eda33b0747c85c14cc2637fcb08975b2c6444398dcd67c40e1863751f8" "q-159585/selection/8d9781a51683d91d91197841e9e786096d99194e4b76add95275d4c164799e4f" "q-159585/selection/9b49ed1a91e9087b6b2cc4f15092d29a6f833d1b3fe90395a973a4df3f6d0b57"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159585" :question/id #uuid "f1184a72-86fc-5f00-a377-62e4c111ae08" :question/math-academy-id "q-159585" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-xy,$ evaluate ${f}_{x}(0,\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-y\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(0,\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡0-\\pi  \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 1-\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\pi -1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-159585/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "facdd9e7-8fcb-5ad1-b9c1-82c0f753df1a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159607/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "85265f94-96ca-55c4-b29a-1fff07b9876c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159607/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "c915c857-4aa5-57b3-a5ae-26f238ebe537" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159607/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "c6a6c5e1-6820-516d-ae49-9649741d2dfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159607/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "6625dd20-5905-51c5-b52c-ecad29453cfd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159607/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "0a7bc5ea-53ea-57c7-bfe5-b72cc7de25fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159607/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "feddb534-ffa7-503c-bdcf-649194d54d6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159607/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-159607/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-159607/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-159607/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-159607/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-159607/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159607" :question/id #uuid "486530c9-71ac-574e-98a1-00908a232a97" :question/math-academy-id "q-159607" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y+{x}^{4}y,$ evaluate ${f}_{y}(\\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y+{x}^{4}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{4}y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡y)+{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (\\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y)+{x}^{4}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y+{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(\\sqrt{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+{(\\sqrt{2})}^{4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1+4 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-159607/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "facdd9e7-8fcb-5ad1-b9c1-82c0f753df1a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159607"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159602/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "a2cf9ca2-1c18-5f6b-a1fb-7bc8e7e0f97d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159602/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "5b8b3741-8173-58d6-b130-4507e7751712" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159602/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "c069a1c5-3593-5dc1-9943-107b76a94416" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159602/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "f74a4074-8c91-5cd0-975f-853eb7053b8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159602/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "6c7f6e4a-bb01-5571-a710-b20be5a112fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159602/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4252601-24c6-56bc-a24a-d2dbe38e9de0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159602/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-159602/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-159602/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-159602/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-159602/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-159602/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159602" :question/id #uuid "b93515d7-933b-5667-83d6-82023485db97" :question/math-academy-id "q-159602" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=4y{x}^{2}-x{y}^{4},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4y{x}^{2}-x{y}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4y{x}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{4}) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)-x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{4}) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}\\cdot (1)-x\\cdot (4{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-4x{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(2,1)} & =4\\cdot {2}^{2}-4\\cdot 2\\cdot {1}^{3} \\\\  & =16-8 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-159602/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "facdd9e7-8fcb-5ad1-b9c1-82c0f753df1a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159602"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159597/selection/674a033d474465d9d9f0df4493c45bcc048338c813d1c1fef462595179d3fcd3" :answer/id #uuid "cbcdb296-8117-5213-bdfa-d455bcf548f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159597/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "fb6c694f-090e-5927-9dcd-fdc9367b9a12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159597/selection/0565f1f20ec34d894ed97519d097802ce8cfc0aa64c42aeae8bbf469ecaccfd7" :answer/id #uuid "28ec4c23-306d-5282-bd15-c90a84a2cd77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159597/selection/2a28a53216361474017108aa9cf0fffd0fb392524d53aeb00b78355e4fa703c6" :answer/id #uuid "d369b486-2ffd-5109-8f0c-5ddf396492e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159597/selection/de65f68b9ebe8220ad685ae8fd317e4e85f600952fac99fcca3864668321a3a0" :answer/id #uuid "3b098e05-9104-5421-8989-7970deaa425b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159597/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "03a157c6-b581-5834-